    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "Forgive my ignorance. But I am supposed to install  treesitter [nvim-treesitter](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter) and LSP [nvim-treesitter](https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter) myself, or is something a functionality similar to Mason or Lazy that come with one of the modules. that will install the language grammars and LSPs? ",
    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Forgive my ignorance. But I am supposed to install  treesitter <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter\">nvim-treesitter</a> and LSP <a href=\"https://github.com/nvim-treesitter/nvim-treesitter\">nvim-treesitter</a> myself, or is something a functionality similar to Mason or Lazy that come with one of the modules. that will install the language grammars and LSPs?</p>",
    "bodyText": "Forgive my ignorance. But I am supposed to install  treesitter nvim-treesitter and LSP nvim-treesitter myself, or is something a functionality similar to Mason or Lazy that come with one of the modules. that will install the language grammars and LSPs?",
